      "created_at": "2013-02-25T12:57:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I dont think so Xchylde - because the components say 'Whenever 7 Damage would be delt in a single round' - versus '1 player&nbsp;<strong>may</strong> skip his turn\" (emphasis mine) - the may implies this is a cost decision, where as the whenever indicates this is a trigger. The difference being you have to choose to do the second so that you can only choose to do this per one card at a time, and the first happens whenever the condition is met - the condition is met by 7 damage to omnitron and so all components can trigger off that.</p>",
